#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""quota-surplus — "use it or lose it": find quota that a window reset will throw away, and tell the leads. No model.

    quota-surplus check [--json] [--dry-run] [--live] [--input FILE]
    quota-surplus notify [--dry-run] [--live] [--input FILE]
    quota-surplus list-work [--repo PATH ...] [--fit frontier|bulk] [--pool POOL] [--json]

djbclark, 2026-11-02: the Gemini 4 Argon weekly window held 25% at 00:30Z and reset at 02:35Z; the operator noticed by hand
and nothing in the fleet would have spent it. This script is the periodic check (launchd, every 15 min, after review:
config/launchd/com.djbclark.quota-surplus.plist); it never dispatches work and never spends quota.

ALGORITHM, per pool and window of `aiuse --available --json` (every field read with .get):
  minutes_left = resets_at - now;   elapsed = window_minutes - minutes_left (at least 5% of the window)
  burn         = pace_ratio * 100 * minutes_left / window_minutes    (pace_ratio = used fraction / elapsed fraction,
                 so this is the burn at the pace so far), else used_percent / elapsed * minutes_left; capped at remaining
  surplus      = remaining_percent - burn                              (what the reset will throw away at this pace)
  alert        when surplus >= min_surplus_pct (15) AND 0 < hours_left <= horizon (6 h for a window of a day or more,
                 1.5 h for a shorter one, the 5-hour windows) AND the pool is usable now
  score        = surplus * weight; weight 2.0 for a frontier pool (a model of [dispatch].frontier_models), 1.5 for a paid
                 subscription, 0.5 for a free pool, 1.0 otherwise; severity `act` when score >= act_score (25), else `info`.
                 A window shorter than a day is `info` at most (it refills all the time; the weekly window binds), and so
                 is a surplus that buys no whole slice at the pool's estimate floor.
  only         pools where running out is fine (djbclark, 2026-11-03): agy (antigravity), omp API credits, codex, zcode
                 (zai), cursor, grok. NEVER the Claude subscription, opencode-go or cline/clinepass, nor any pool not
                 named. Also skipped: other `credits` rows, a service the routing marks never_route or operator_gated,
                 access `forbidden`, retired, or one in aiuse [disabled_services].
  no verdict   a stale or missing reading (aiuse `fresh` false or `stale` true; its `stale_reason` is reported), a window
                 without resets_at or window_minutes, a window aiuse marks `exhausted` (an agent-reported refusal beats
                 its percentage), and after a reset time passes until a reading collected after it shows the NEW
                 resets_at (2026-11-02: Argon still refused 5 min after aiuse dropped the window). Never an alert.
A repo-scoped pool (opencode-go: techno-euphora and Hermes only; route_agent's allow_repos/allow_seats when the routing
has them) is offered only to leads and work lists of the repos and seats on its list.

`check` records each alert's first sighting in the state file (~/.local/state/quota-surplus/state.json, written
atomically; not with --dry-run). An episode is the pool + window + resets_at (a resets_at within 10 minutes of a recorded
one is the same episode); a new resets_at is a new episode. `notify` sends each new `act` episode ONCE, and a pool at
most once per renotify_h (24 h) across episodes: one hermes-ping, and one relay.py line (`--fyi`, never `--steer`;
`--idle 1800` for a Claude Paseo target) to each live lead seat (a fleet.py row whose name or title starts with the word
`LEAD` in capitals, plus any agent id in QUOTA_SURPLUS_LEADS, comma-separated, e.g. a `/helm lead` session). An episode
counts as paged only when hermes-ping exited 0. Each lead counts as reached only on relay's `delivered` (relay runs with
--json, detached through `quota-surplus _relay-run OUT -- ARGV`, which records its exit status and JSON result in
~/.local/state/quota-surplus/relays/, so an --idle wait never holds the timer). A `queued` send with a record id is
followed on later runs with `relay.py --status ID --json`: `delivered` marks the lead; `failed` or `expired` allows ONE
re-send per lead per episode; `queued`/`sending` is never re-sent (it would duplicate). `accepted`, `unverified` or
`queued` without a record is final: not reached, never re-sent. A relay that never sent (refused, runner failed or
abandoned) is retried, up to 3 attempts; a failed ping is retried each run (log: ~/.local/state/quota-surplus/relay.log).
A corrupt state file is kept aside as state.json.corrupt and the run starts from empty state (at most one repeat page
per open episode).
`notify --dry-run` prints what it would send and sends nothing.
The relay line advises at most N concurrent slices (surplus // the pool's route_agent estimate floor, 0 = do not dispatch;
else 1-2; never above
its max_parallel), a `check --live` between them, and that a provider's "Usage Limit Reached" overrides aiuse (aiuse lags
a burst: 2026-11-03, four parallel agy runs spent a 25% Argon surplus in ~10 min while aiuse still read 25%).

`list-work` reads docs/surplus-work.md in each repo under ~/src (or each --repo), most valuable first (format: that file
in djbclark-ade); `--pool POOL` (a service or provider/family) keeps only items that pool may serve: its fit and, for a
repo-scoped pool, its repos. Exit: 0 done, 2 usage (an unknown --pool too), 3 aiuse unreadable (no verdict, nothing sent
or recorded), 75 another check/notify held `<state>.lock` past QUOTA_SURPLUS_LOCK_TIMEOUT (300 s; nothing read, sent or
recorded). check and notify (not --dry-run) hold that lock for their whole read-modify-write of the state file.
Environment: QUOTA_SURPLUS_STATE, QUOTA_SURPLUS_PING (hermes-ping), QUOTA_SURPLUS_RELAY (relay.py), QUOTA_SURPLUS_FLEET
(fleet.py), QUOTA_SURPLUS_LEADS, QUOTA_SURPLUS_SRC (~/src), QUOTA_SURPLUS_NOW (ISO time, tests), QUOTA_SURPLUS_MIN_SURPLUS,
_ACT_SCORE, _HORIZON_WEEKLY_H, _HORIZON_SHORT_H, _RENOTIFY_H, _LOCK_TIMEOUT.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import importlib.machinery
import importlib.util
import fcntl
import json
import os
import re
import shlex
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
import time
from dataclasses import dataclass, field
from datetime import UTC, datetime, timedelta
from pathlib import Path
from typing import Any

HERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
REPO = HERE.parent
HOME = Path.home()

MIN_SURPLUS_PCT = 15.0
ACT_SCORE = 25.0
HORIZON_WEEKLY_H = 6.0
HORIZON_SHORT_H = 1.5
EPISODE_TOLERANCE_S = 600
RENOTIFY_H = 24.0
LOCK_TIMEOUT_S = 300.0
WEIGHT = {"frontier": 2.0, "subscription": 1.5, "free": 0.5}
NO_ALERT_BILLING = {"credits", "prepaid"}
# djbclark's ruling (2026-11-03, via lead 7c58015b): running out is fine on these aiuse providers, never on the others.
EXHAUST_OK = frozenset({"antigravity", "omp", "codex", "zai", "cursor", "grok", "grok-bot"})
NEVER_EXHAUST = frozenset({"claude", "opencode-go", "cline", "clinepass"})
# Fallback scope while the routing has no allow_repos/allow_seats (PR 260): djbclark, 2026-11-02. cline/clinepass need
# none here: NEVER_EXHAUST and the routing's never_route/operator_gated already keep them out of every alert.
DEFAULT_SCOPES = {"opencode-go": (("techno-euphora",), ("hermes",))}
SURPLUS_FILE = "docs/surplus-work.md"
# Strict: the word LEAD in capitals at the start of the seat's name or title ("LEAD paseo-only rearch"), not "Lead review".
LEAD_RE = re.compile(r"^LEAD(\s|$)")


def env_float(name: str, default: float) -> float:
    try:
        return float(os.environ.get(name, default))
    except ValueError:
        return default


def now_utc() -> datetime:
    raw = os.environ.get("QUOTA_SURPLUS_NOW")
    return parse_ts(raw) or datetime.now(UTC) if raw else datetime.now(UTC)


def parse_ts(value: Any) -> datetime | None:
    if not value:
        return None
    try:
        d = datetime.fromisoformat(str(value).replace("Z", "+00:00"))
    except ValueError:
        return None
    return d if d.tzinfo else d.replace(tzinfo=UTC)


# -- policy: what the routing says about each pool ------------------------------------------

@dataclass
class PoolPolicy:
    service: str
    billing: str = ""
    frontier: bool = False
    blocked: str | None = None              # why it is never alerted, or None
    kinds: tuple[str, ...] = ()
    dispatch: str = ""
    allow_repos: tuple[str, ...] = ()
    allow_seats: tuple[str, ...] = ()
    max_parallel: int = 1
    slice_cost: float | None = None         # percent of the binding window one slice uses (route_agent estimate floor)


@dataclass
class Policy:
    pools: dict[tuple[str, str | None], PoolPolicy] = field(default_factory=dict)
    disabled: set[str] = field(default_factory=set)
    never: set[str] = field(default_factory=set)

    def for_row(self, provider: str, family: str | None) -> PoolPolicy:
        return (self.pools.get((provider, family)) or self.pools.get((provider, None))
                or PoolPolicy(service=provider, blocked="routing never_route/operator_gated"
                              if provider in self.never else None))


# Dispatch lines a lead should use, where the router's generic line is not the one that works today.
DISPATCH_OVERRIDE = {
    # acp-dispatch cannot read a fresh Argon window yet (2026-11-02), so it refuses Argon; acp-run does not ask.
    "antigravity-argon": "acp-run agy --model gemini-4-argon --effort high",
}


def load_route_agent():
    path = HERE / "route_agent.py"
    loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader("route_agent_qs", str(path))
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_loader("route_agent_qs", loader)
    mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    sys.modules["route_agent_qs"] = mod
    loader.exec_module(mod)
    return mod


def policy_from_routing(aiuse_disabled: dict | None = None) -> Policy:
    ra = load_route_agent()
    pub = ra.policy_public()
    frontier_tokens = [str(t).lower() for t in ((pub.get("dispatch") or {}).get("frontier_models") or [])]
    never = set((pub.get("discovery") or {}).get("never_route") or [])
    never |= set((pub.get("discovery") or {}).get("operator_gated") or [])
    never |= set((pub.get("dispatch") or {}).get("operator_gated") or [])
    pol = Policy(disabled=set(ra.operator_disabled()) | set((aiuse_disabled or {}).keys()), never=never)
    for svc in ra.SERVICES:
        models = dict(getattr(svc, "models", {}) or {})
        frontier = any(tok in str(m).lower() for m in models.values() for tok in frontier_tokens)
        blocked = None
        if svc.name in never:
            blocked = "routing never_route/operator_gated"
        elif getattr(svc, "access", "") == "forbidden":
            blocked = "access forbidden"
        elif getattr(svc, "retired", False):
            blocked = "retired"
        elif getattr(svc, "billing", "") in NO_ALERT_BILLING and svc.name not in EXHAUST_OK:
            blocked = f"{svc.billing}: prepaid credits roll over"
        kinds = tuple(sorted(models, key=lambda k: (k != "frontier", (svc.good_at or {}).get(k, 99))))
        agent = getattr(svc, "agent", "") or svc.name
        first = kinds[0] if kinds else ""
        # routing values are "<model> [--effort LEVEL]"; a model id may hold a backslash (zai's builtin:...\GLM-5.3), so
        # the printed line is shell-quoted per argument (local-review P2 on 911bf68)
        dispatch = DISPATCH_OVERRIDE.get(svc.name) or (
            shlex.join(["acp-run", agent, "--model", *str(models[first]).split()]) if first else "")
        repos, seats = routing_scope(svc)
        first_model = models.get(first, "")
        try:
            cost = ra.floor_lookup((pub.get("dispatch") or {}).get("estimate_floor") or {}, svc.name, first or None,
                                   any(tok in first_model.lower() for tok in frontier_tokens))
        except (AttributeError, TypeError, ValueError):
            cost = None
        pp = PoolPolicy(service=svc.name, billing=getattr(svc, "billing", ""), frontier=frontier, blocked=blocked,
                        kinds=kinds, dispatch=dispatch, allow_repos=repos, allow_seats=seats,
                        max_parallel=int(getattr(svc, "max_parallel", 1) or 1), slice_cost=cost)
        key = tuple(svc.pool) if getattr(svc, "pool", None) else (svc.name, None)
        pol.pools[key] = pp
    return pol


def routing_scope(svc: Any, name: str | None = None) -> tuple[tuple[str, ...], tuple[str, ...]]:
    """(allow_repos, allow_seats) of a routing service: the one adapter onto route_agent's repo scope.

    TODO(route-repo-scope): once that slice (PR 260, `[[service]] allow_repos/allow_seats`, `Service.scope_block`) is on
    master, the getattr path is the only one; delete DEFAULT_SCOPES and this fallback. Until then the operator's rulings
    (opencode-go and cline/clinepass: techno-euphora and Hermes only) are the fallback."""
    repos = tuple(str(r).lower() for r in (getattr(svc, "allow_repos", ()) or ()))
    seats = tuple(str(s).lower() for s in (getattr(svc, "allow_seats", ()) or ()))
    if repos or seats:
        return repos, seats
    return DEFAULT_SCOPES.get(name or getattr(svc, "name", ""), ((), ()))


# -- the algorithm ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

def expected_burn(w: dict, minutes_left: float, window_minutes: float) -> float | None:
    """Percent the window will burn until reset at the pace so far, capped at what remains; None when unknowable."""
    remaining = w.get("remaining_percent")
    if remaining is None:
        return None
    pace = w.get("pace_ratio")
    if isinstance(pace, (int, float)):
        burn = float(pace) * 100.0 * minutes_left / window_minutes
    else:
        used = w.get("used_percent")
        if used is None:
            used = 100.0 - float(remaining)
        elapsed = max(window_minutes - minutes_left, 0.05 * window_minutes)
        burn = float(used) / elapsed * minutes_left
    return max(0.0, min(burn, float(remaining)))


def ruling_block(provider: str) -> str | None:
    """Why djbclark's 2026-11-03 ruling keeps `provider` out of every alert, or None (running out is fine there)."""
    if provider in NEVER_EXHAUST:
        return f"djbclark 2026-11-03: running out is never fine on {provider}"
    if provider not in EXHAUST_OK:
        return "not on djbclark's 2026-11-03 run-out-is-fine list"
    return None


def window_key(pool: str, label: Any) -> str:
    return f"{pool}|{label}"


def assess(data: dict, policy: Policy, now: datetime, *, min_surplus: float = MIN_SURPLUS_PCT,
           act_score: float = ACT_SCORE, horizon_weekly_h: float = HORIZON_WEEKLY_H,
           horizon_short_h: float = HORIZON_SHORT_H, state: dict | None = None) -> list[dict]:
    """One verdict per pool window: verdict `alert` (with severity), `none`, `skip` or `no-verdict`.

    `state` (the state file) supplies each window's last resets_at seen in the future: once that time has passed, a
    window has no verdict until a reading collected after it shows a NEW resets_at."""
    out: list[dict] = []
    seen_resets = (state or {}).get("windows") if isinstance((state or {}).get("windows"), dict) else {}
    disabled = set(policy.disabled) | set((data.get("disabled_services") or {}).keys())
    seen: set[tuple[str, str | None]] = set()
    for row in data.get("available") or []:
        if not isinstance(row, dict):
            continue
        provider = str(row.get("provider") or "?")
        family = row.get("pool_family")
        pp = policy.for_row(provider, family)
        pool = f"{provider}/{family}" if family else provider
        seen |= {(provider, family), (provider, None)}
        base = {"pool": pool, "service": pp.service, "provider": provider, "pool_family": family,
                "frontier": pp.frontier, "billing": pp.billing, "dispatch": pp.dispatch, "kinds": list(pp.kinds),
                "allow_repos": list(pp.allow_repos), "allow_seats": list(pp.allow_seats),
                "max_parallel": pp.max_parallel, "slice_cost": pp.slice_cost}
        windows = [w for w in (row.get("windows") or []) if isinstance(w, dict)]
        credits = (row.get("binding_window") == "credits" or any(w.get("label") == "credits" for w in windows))
        reason = ruling_block(provider)
        if reason:
            pass
        elif credits and pp.billing not in NO_ALERT_BILLING:
            # a credits row is an expiring grant only for a service the routing bills as credits (omp's API grant,
            # which the ruling lets run out); any other credits balance rolls over
            reason = "credits: prepaid credits roll over"
        elif pp.blocked:
            reason = pp.blocked
        elif pp.service in disabled or provider in disabled:
            reason = "aiuse [disabled_services]"
        if reason:
            out.append({**base, "window": row.get("binding_window"), "verdict": "skip", "reason": reason})
            continue
        if row.get("fresh") is False or row.get("stale") is True or not windows:
            why = row.get("stale_reason") or (f"reading {row.get('age_seconds')} s old" if windows else "no windows")
            out.append({**base, "window": row.get("binding_window"), "verdict": "no-verdict",
                        "reason": f"stale reading: {why}" if windows else "missing reading", "stale_reason":
                        row.get("stale_reason")})
            continue
        usable = row.get("usable_now") is not False
        collected = parse_ts(row.get("collected_at"))
        for w in windows:
            label = w.get("label")
            reset = parse_ts(w.get("resets_at"))
            wm = w.get("window_minutes")
            rem = w.get("remaining_percent")
            item = {**base, "window": label, "resets_at": w.get("resets_at"), "remaining_percent": rem,
                    "window_minutes": wm, "pace_ratio": w.get("pace_ratio")}
            if reset is None or not wm or rem is None:
                out.append({**item, "verdict": "no-verdict", "reason": "window lacks resets_at/window_minutes/remaining"})
                continue
            minutes_left = (reset - now).total_seconds() / 60.0
            hours_left = minutes_left / 60.0
            item["hours_left"] = round(hours_left, 2)
            if minutes_left <= 0:
                out.append({**item, "verdict": "no-verdict", "reason": "reset already passed: stale reading"})
                continue
            prev = parse_ts(((seen_resets or {}).get(window_key(pool, label)) or {}).get("resets_at"))
            if prev is not None and prev <= now:
                # 2026-11-02: Argon still refused 5 min after aiuse dropped the window; only a reading taken after the
                # reset that shows the NEW resets_at proves the headroom is back.
                if reset <= prev + timedelta(seconds=EPISODE_TOLERANCE_S):
                    out.append({**item, "verdict": "no-verdict", "reset_hold": True,
                                "reason": f"reset at {prev.isoformat()} passed; waiting for a reading with the new resets_at"})
                    continue
                if collected is None or collected < prev:
                    out.append({**item, "verdict": "no-verdict", "reset_hold": True,
                                "reason": f"reading collected before the reset at {prev.isoformat()}"})
                    continue
            if str(w.get("state") or "") == "exhausted":
                out.append({**item, "verdict": "no-verdict",
                            "reason": "aiuse marks the window exhausted (a provider refusal beats its percentage)"})
                continue
            burn = expected_burn(w, minutes_left, float(wm))
            if burn is None:
                out.append({**item, "verdict": "no-verdict", "reason": "no remaining_percent"})
                continue
            surplus = float(rem) - burn
            short = float(wm) < 1440
            horizon = horizon_short_h if short else horizon_weekly_h
            weight = WEIGHT["frontier"] if pp.frontier else WEIGHT.get(pp.billing, 1.0)
            score = surplus * weight
            item.update(expected_burn=round(burn, 1), surplus=round(surplus, 1), horizon_h=horizon,
                        weight=weight, score=round(score, 1))
            buys_none = bool(pp.slice_cost) and surplus < float(pp.slice_cost or 0)
            if not usable:
                out.append({**item, "verdict": "none", "reason": "not usable now"})
            elif hours_left > horizon:
                out.append({**item, "verdict": "none", "reason": f"reset in {hours_left:.1f} h > horizon {horizon:g} h"})
            elif surplus < min_surplus:
                out.append({**item, "verdict": "none", "reason": f"surplus {surplus:.1f}% < {min_surplus:g}%"})
            else:
                act = score >= act_score and not short and not buys_none
                why = " (a window under a day)" if short and score >= act_score else (
                    " (buys no whole slice)" if buys_none and score >= act_score else "")
                out.append({**item, "verdict": "alert", "severity": "act" if act else "info", "info_why": why})
    # A frontier pool missing from `--available` (aiuse drops an exhausted or unusable pool, 2026-11-03: Argon after an
    # agent-reported quota refusal) has no reading: say so, so its absence is not read as "nothing to spend".
    for (prov, fam), pp in policy.pools.items():
        if (pp.frontier and not pp.blocked and (prov, fam) not in seen and prov not in disabled
                and pp.service not in disabled and ruling_block(prov) is None):
            out.append({"pool": f"{prov}/{fam}" if fam else prov, "service": pp.service, "provider": prov,
                        "pool_family": fam, "frontier": True, "window": None, "verdict": "no-verdict",
                        "reason": "no reading in aiuse --available (exhausted, excluded or not collected)"})
    return out


# -- state: one alert per pool per window episode ---------------------------------------------

def state_path() -> Path:
    return Path(os.environ.get("QUOTA_SURPLUS_STATE") or HOME / ".local/state/quota-surplus/state.json")


def load_state(keep_aside: bool = True) -> dict:
    """The state file, or empty state. A corrupt file is kept aside as `<name>.corrupt` (never silently overwritten;
    with keep_aside False, a dry run, it is left in place)."""
    empty = {"episodes": {}, "windows": {}, "pools": {}}
    p = state_path()
    try:
        raw = p.read_text()
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return empty
    except OSError as e:
        print(f"quota-surplus: cannot read {p}: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return empty
    try:
        d = json.loads(raw)
    except ValueError:
        d = None
    if not isinstance(d, dict) or not isinstance(d.get("episodes"), dict):
        if keep_aside:
            try:
                os.replace(p, p.with_name(p.name + ".corrupt"))
            except OSError:
                pass
        print(f"quota-surplus: corrupt state {p}" + (f" kept as {p.name}.corrupt" if keep_aside else "")
              + "; starting from empty state", file=sys.stderr)
        return empty
    for k in ("windows", "pools"):
        if not isinstance(d.get(k), dict):
            d[k] = {}
    return d


def save_state(state: dict) -> None:
    p = state_path()
    p.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    fd, tmp = tempfile.mkstemp(prefix=p.name + ".", suffix=".tmp", dir=p.parent)
    try:
        with os.fdopen(fd, "w") as f:
            json.dump(state, f, indent=2, sort_keys=True)
            f.write("\n")
        os.replace(tmp, p)
    except BaseException:
        try:
            os.unlink(tmp)
        except OSError:
            pass
        raise


def episode_of(state: dict, alert: dict) -> str:
    """The episode key for `alert`: an existing one of the same pool/window whose resets_at is within tolerance, else new."""
    pool_key = f"{alert['pool']}|{alert.get('window')}"
    reset = parse_ts(alert.get("resets_at"))
    for key, ep in (state.get("episodes") or {}).items():
        if not isinstance(ep, dict) or ep.get("pool_key") != pool_key:
            continue
        other = parse_ts(ep.get("resets_at"))
        if reset and other and abs((reset - other).total_seconds()) <= EPISODE_TOLERANCE_S:
            return key
    return f"{pool_key}|{alert.get('resets_at')}"


def record(state: dict, verdicts: list[dict], now: datetime) -> None:
    """Note each window's future resets_at (for the reset-passed rule) and each alert's episode."""
    wins = state.setdefault("windows", {})
    for v in verdicts:
        r = parse_ts(v.get("resets_at"))
        # a reading held by the reset-passed rule must not move the baseline it failed against (local-review P2)
        if r is not None and r > now and not v.get("reset_hold"):
            wins[window_key(v["pool"], v.get("window"))] = {"resets_at": v.get("resets_at"), "seen_at": now.isoformat()}
    eps = state.setdefault("episodes", {})
    for a in (v for v in verdicts if v.get("verdict") == "alert"):
        key = episode_of(state, a)
        a["episode"] = key
        ep = eps.setdefault(key, {"pool_key": f"{a['pool']}|{a.get('window')}", "resets_at": a.get("resets_at"),
                                  "first_seen": now.isoformat()})
        ep["last_seen"] = now.isoformat()
        ep["severity"] = a.get("severity")
        ep["surplus"] = a.get("surplus")
        a["notified_at"] = ep.get("notified_at")
    # prune episodes a day past their reset, and window marks a week past theirs
    for key in [k for k, ep in eps.items() if isinstance(ep, dict) and (r := parse_ts(ep.get("resets_at")))
                and (now - r).total_seconds() > 86400]:
        del eps[key]
    for key in [k for k, w in wins.items() if isinstance(w, dict) and (r := parse_ts(w.get("resets_at")))
                and (now - r).total_seconds() > 8 * 86400]:
        del wins[key]


# -- aiuse ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

def read_aiuse(live: bool, input_path: str | None) -> dict | None:
    if input_path:
        try:
            d = json.loads(Path(input_path).read_text())
        except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
            print(f"quota-surplus: cannot read {input_path}: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
            return None
        return d if isinstance(d, dict) else None
    argv = ["aiuse", "--available", "--json"] + (["--live"] if live else [])
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(argv, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=300, check=False, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as e:
        print(f"quota-surplus: aiuse failed: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return None
    if r.returncode != 0:
        print(f"quota-surplus: aiuse exited {r.returncode}: {r.stderr.strip()[:300]}", file=sys.stderr)
        return None
    try:
        d = json.loads(r.stdout)
    except ValueError:
        print("quota-surplus: aiuse printed no JSON", file=sys.stderr)
        return None
    return d if isinstance(d, dict) else None


# -- surplus work lists ---------------------------------------------------------------------

ITEM_RE = re.compile(r"^\s*(\d+)\.\s+(.*)$")
VALUE_RANK = {"high": 3, "medium": 2, "med": 2, "low": 1}


def parse_work(text: str, repo: str) -> list[dict]:
    """Items `N. task | kind: K | size: S | fit: frontier | read-only: yes | value: high` of a surplus-work.md."""
    items = []
    for line in text.splitlines():
        m = ITEM_RE.match(line)
        if not m or "|" not in m.group(2):
            continue
        parts = [p.strip() for p in m.group(2).split("|")]
        item: dict[str, Any] = {"repo": repo, "n": int(m.group(1)), "task": parts[0]}
        for p in parts[1:]:
            if ":" in p:
                k, v = p.split(":", 1)
                item[k.strip().lower()] = v.strip()
        item["fit"] = [f.strip().lower() for f in str(item.get("fit") or "any").split(",") if f.strip()]
        item["read_only"] = str(item.pop("read-only", "no")).lower() in ("yes", "y", "true")
        items.append(item)
    return items


def repo_name(path: Path) -> str:
    """The repository's name: the last part of its origin remote, else the directory name."""
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(path), "remote", "get-url", "origin"], capture_output=True, text=True,
                           timeout=10, check=False, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)
        url = r.stdout.strip() if r.returncode == 0 else ""
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        url = ""
    name = url.rstrip("/").rsplit("/", 1)[-1].rsplit(":", 1)[-1] if url else path.name
    return name.removesuffix(".git")


def find_work(repos: list[Path] | None = None) -> list[dict]:
    """Every item of every docs/surplus-work.md, one copy per repository (worktrees of a repo are skipped as copies)."""
    if repos is None:
        src = Path(os.environ.get("QUOTA_SURPLUS_SRC") or HOME / "src")
        repos = sorted(p for p in src.iterdir() if p.is_dir()) if src.is_dir() else []
    seen: dict[str, Path] = {}
    for p in repos:
        f = p / SURPLUS_FILE
        if not f.is_file():
            continue
        name = repo_name(p)
        # the primary checkout (directory named like the repo) wins over a worktree of it
        if name in seen and seen[name].name == name:
            continue
        seen[name] = p
    items: list[dict] = []
    for name, p in seen.items():
        try:
            items += [dict(i, path=str(p / SURPLUS_FILE)) for i in parse_work((p / SURPLUS_FILE).read_text(), name)]
        except OSError:
            continue
    items.sort(key=lambda i: (-VALUE_RANK.get(str(i.get("value", "")).lower(), 0), not i["read_only"], i["repo"],
                              i["n"]))
    return items


def in_scope(alert: dict, repo: str | None, seat: str | None = None) -> bool:
    repos, seats = alert.get("allow_repos") or [], alert.get("allow_seats") or []
    if not repos and not seats:
        return True
    return bool((repo and repo.lower() in repos) or (seat and seat.lower() in seats))


def work_for(alert: dict, items: list[dict]) -> list[dict]:
    fit = "frontier" if alert.get("frontier") else "bulk"
    return [i for i in items if in_scope(alert, i["repo"]) and (fit in i["fit"] or "any" in i["fit"])]


# -- notify ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

def local_reset(alert: dict, now: datetime) -> str:
    r = parse_ts(alert.get("resets_at"))
    if not r:
        return "?"
    return f"{r.astimezone().strftime('%a %H:%M %Z')} (in {(r - now).total_seconds() / 3600:.1f}h)"


def kinds_phrase(alert: dict) -> str:
    if alert.get("frontier"):
        return "frontier read-only reviews, second opinions, design"
    return ", ".join(alert.get("kinds") or []) or "any work it is routed for"


def ping_text(alert: dict, now: datetime) -> str:
    return (f"quota surplus: {alert['pool']} {float(alert['remaining_percent']):.0f}% left, resets "
            f"{local_reset(alert, now)}: use it for {kinds_phrase(alert)}")


def slice_advice(alert: dict) -> tuple[int, int | None]:
    """(at most N concurrent slices, about M slices in total or None).

    Lead 7c58015b, 2026-11-03: four parallel read-only agy runs spent a 25% Argon surplus in ~10 minutes while aiuse still
    read 25%: aiuse lags a burst, and a percentage does not say how many slices it buys. With a per-slice cost
    (route_agent's estimate floor for the pool's first kind) the surplus buys surplus // cost slices; without one, 1-2.
    Never more than the pool's max_parallel."""
    cap = max(1, int(alert.get("max_parallel") or 1))
    cost = alert.get("slice_cost")
    if cost:
        total = max(0, int(float(alert.get("surplus") or 0) // float(cost)))
        return min(cap, total), total
    return min(2, cap), None


def relay_text(alert: dict, now: datetime, n_work: int) -> str:
    n, total = slice_advice(alert)
    buys = f" (it buys about {total} at ~{alert['slice_cost']:g}% each)" if total is not None else ""
    advice = (f"Run at most {n} concurrent slice{'s' if n != 1 else ''}{buys} and re-check `quota-surplus check --live` "
              f"between them" if n else
              f"It buys no whole slice{buys}: do not dispatch to it")
    return (f"quota surplus (use it or lose it): {alert['pool']} ({alert.get('window')}) has "
            f"{float(alert['remaining_percent']):.0f}% left and resets {local_reset(alert, now)}; about "
            f"{alert['surplus']:.0f}% will be lost at the current pace. Dispatch line: {alert.get('dispatch') or '?'}. "
            f"{advice}: aiuse lags a burst, and a provider 'Usage Limit Reached' overrides its reading. "
            f"Pick read-only items that finish before the reset: `quota-surplus list-work --pool "
            f"{alert.get('service') or alert['pool']}` ({n_work} items in docs/surplus-work.md lists); "
            f"skill quota-surplus. FYI, no reply needed.")


def lead_seats(fleet_rows: list[dict], extra_ids: list[str] | None = None) -> list[dict]:
    """Live seats whose name or title starts with the word LEAD in capitals, plus the ids in QUOTA_SURPLUS_LEADS."""
    if extra_ids is None:
        extra_ids = [s.strip() for s in os.environ.get("QUOTA_SURPLUS_LEADS", "").split(",") if s.strip()]
    seats = []
    for r in fleet_rows:
        if not isinstance(r, dict) or r.get("finished") or r.get("status") in ("closed", "finished", "archived"):
            continue
        if (LEAD_RE.match(str(r.get("name") or "")) or LEAD_RE.match(str(r.get("title") or ""))
                or str(r.get("id") or "") in extra_ids):
            seats.append(r)
    return seats


def relay_argv(relay: str, row: dict, text: str) -> list[str]:
    # --json: the outcome is read from relay's structured result, never from its exit status (exit 0 also means
    # `queued`/`accepted`; `unverified` exits 1 although the text may have arrived)
    argv = [sys.executable, relay, str(row.get("id")), text, "--fyi", "--json"]
    if row.get("host") == "paseo" and row.get("agent") == "claude":
        argv += ["--idle", "1800"]      # a Claude Paseo target is steered: wait for idle (helm lead.md section 0 item 5)
    return argv


def fleet_rows() -> list[dict]:
    fleet = os.environ.get("QUOTA_SURPLUS_FLEET") or str(REPO / "skills/session-finder/fleet.py")
    try:
        r = subprocess.run([sys.executable, fleet, "--json"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=120, check=False,
                           stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)
        rows = json.loads(r.stdout) if r.returncode == 0 else []
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError, ValueError):
        rows = []
    return rows if isinstance(rows, list) else []


def seat_scope(row: dict) -> tuple[str | None, str | None]:
    cwd = row.get("cwd")
    repo = repo_name(Path(cwd)) if cwd and Path(cwd).is_dir() else (Path(cwd).name if cwd else None)
    seat = "hermes" if row.get("agent") == "hermes" else None
    return repo, seat


def send_ping(text: str) -> bool:
    exe = os.environ.get("QUOTA_SURPLUS_PING") or str(HOME / ".local/bin/hermes-ping")
    try:
        r = subprocess.run([exe, text], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=120, check=False,
                           stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as e:
        print(f"quota-surplus: ping failed: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return False
    if r.returncode != 0:
        print(f"quota-surplus: ping exited {r.returncode}: {r.stderr.strip()[:200]}", file=sys.stderr)
    return r.returncode == 0


MAX_RELAY_ATTEMPTS = 3
RELAY_RUN_TIMEOUT_S = 2400        # _relay-run's own bound on relay.py (above relay's --idle 1800)


def spawn_relay(argv: list[str], out: str) -> bool:
    """Start relay.py detached through this script's `_relay-run`, which writes relay's exit status to `out` when it ends
    (an --idle 1800 wait must not hold the 15-minute timer; the plist sets AbandonProcessGroup). True when it started;
    delivery is judged later from `out` (relay_outcome), never from the launch (AGENTS.md order 10)."""
    log = state_path().parent / "relay.log"
    try:
        log.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        with log.open("a") as fh:
            fh.write(f"{datetime.now(UTC).isoformat()} {json.dumps(argv[2:])}\n")
            fh.flush()
            # relay.py refuses a sender it cannot name (exit 4); a launchd run has no session, so declare one
            env = dict(os.environ, RELAY_SENDER_NAME=os.environ.get("RELAY_SENDER_NAME") or "quota-surplus")
            subprocess.Popen([sys.executable, str(Path(__file__).resolve()), "_relay-run", out, "--", *argv],
                             stdout=fh, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL,
                             start_new_session=True, env=env)
    except OSError as e:
        print(f"quota-surplus: relay failed to start: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return False
    return True


def last_json(text: str) -> dict | None:
    """The last line of TEXT that parses as a JSON object (relay --json prints one), or None."""
    for line in reversed((text or "").splitlines()):
        line = line.strip()
        if line.startswith("{"):
            try:
                d = json.loads(line)
            except ValueError:
                continue
            if isinstance(d, dict):
                return d
    return None


def relay_run(out: str, argv: list[str]) -> int:
    """`_relay-run OUT -- ARGV`: run relay.py to its end and record its exit status and its --json result in OUT
    (atomically)."""
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(argv, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=RELAY_RUN_TIMEOUT_S, check=False,
                           stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)
        rec = {"rc": r.returncode, "json": last_json(r.stdout), "tail": r.stderr[-500:]}
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as e:
        rec = {"rc": 127, "json": None, "tail": str(e)[:500]}
    p = Path(out)
    tmp = p.with_name(p.name + ".tmp")
    tmp.write_text(json.dumps(rec))
    os.replace(tmp, p)
    return 0


def relay_outcome(out: str | None) -> dict | None:
    """The runner's record {"rc", "json"} from its outcome file, or None while it runs (no file yet)."""
    try:
        d = json.loads(Path(out).read_text()) if out else None
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None
    if not isinstance(d, dict):
        return {"rc": 1, "json": None}
    return {"rc": d.get("rc") if isinstance(d.get("rc"), int) else 1,
            "json": d.get("json") if isinstance(d.get("json"), dict) else None}


def classify_send(outcome: dict) -> tuple[str, str | None]:
    """What one relay.py send did, from its --json result: ("delivered", None), ("deferred", record id),
    ("unconfirmed", None) or ("not-sent", None). Only `delivered` is a delivery (AGENTS.md order 10).

    `unconfirmed` (result accepted, queued or unverified, or a queued answer without a record id) may have reached the
    lead and has nothing to follow up: it is never counted and never resent, since a resend could duplicate it.
    `not-sent` (no JSON result: relay refused before sending, or the runner failed) is safe to retry."""
    j = outcome.get("json") or {}
    if j.get("queued") or j.get("state") == "queued":
        rid = j.get("record")
        return ("deferred", str(rid)) if rid else ("unconfirmed", None)
    result = j.get("result")
    if result == "delivered":
        return "delivered", None
    if result is not None or j.get("sent") is True:
        return "unconfirmed", None
    return "not-sent", None


def relay_status(relay_py: str, rid: str) -> str | None:
    """A deferred record's state from `relay.py --status RID --json` (queued, sending, delivered, failed, expired,
    cancelled), "missing" when relay no longer has it, None when relay could not be read (try again next run)."""
    try:
        r = subprocess.run([sys.executable, relay_py, "--status", rid, "--json"], capture_output=True, text=True,
                           timeout=60, check=False, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return None
    j = last_json(r.stdout)
    if j is None:
        return None
    if j.get("found") is False:
        return "missing"
    st = j.get("state")
    return str(st) if r.returncode == 0 and st else None


def in_cooldown(state: dict, pool: str, now: datetime, renotify_h: float, episode: str | None = None) -> bool:
    """True when `pool` was paged within renotify_h for an episode other than `episode`."""
    rec = (state.get("pools") or {}).get(pool) or {}
    last = parse_ts(rec.get("notified_at"))
    return last is not None and rec.get("episode") != episode and (now - last).total_seconds() < renotify_h * 3600


def notify(alerts: list[dict], state: dict, now: datetime, *, dry_run: bool, rows: list[dict] | None = None,
           items: list[dict] | None = None, ping=send_ping, relay=spawn_relay, status=relay_status,
           renotify_h: float = RENOTIFY_H) -> list[dict]:
    """Page each new `act` episode once, a pool at most once per renotify_h. Returns the actions (sent or planned).

    The operator ping and each lead relay are tracked separately, and none counts until it is known to have succeeded:
    the episode's `notified_at` (and the pool cooldown) only after hermes-ping exits 0; a lead's `delivered_at` only on a
    `delivered` result. A relay that relay.py deferred (`queued`, with a record id) is followed on later runs through
    `relay.py --status ID --json`: delivered marks it; failed or expired allows ONE re-send per lead per episode;
    queued or sending is left alone (a re-send would duplicate it); cancelled or gone ends it. A result relay could not
    confirm (accepted, queued without a record, unverified) is final: not delivered, never resent. A relay that never
    sent (refused, runner failed or abandoned) is retried, up to MAX_RELAY_ATTEMPTS."""
    actions: list[dict] = []
    eps = state.setdefault("episodes", {})
    todo = [a for a in alerts if a.get("verdict") == "alert" and a.get("severity") == "act"]
    if not todo:
        return actions
    rows = fleet_rows() if rows is None else rows
    items = find_work() if items is None else items
    relay_py = os.environ.get("QUOTA_SURPLUS_RELAY") or str(REPO / "skills/session-finder/relay.py")
    planned: set[str] = set()
    for a in todo:
        ep = eps.setdefault(a["episode"], {})
        if in_cooldown(state, a["pool"], now, renotify_h, a["episode"]) or a["pool"] in planned:
            if not ep.get("notified_at"):
                actions.append({"episode": a.get("episode"), "action": "cooldown", "pool": a["pool"]})
            continue
        planned.add(a["pool"])
        if not ep.get("notified_at"):
            text = ping_text(a, now)
            actions.append({"episode": a.get("episode"), "action": "ping", "text": text})
            if not dry_run:
                if ping(text):
                    ep["notified_at"] = now.isoformat()
                    state.setdefault("pools", {})[a["pool"]] = {"notified_at": now.isoformat(), "episode": a["episode"]}
                else:
                    ep["failed_at"] = now.isoformat()
                    actions.append({"episode": a.get("episode"), "action": "failed"})
        n_work = len(work_for(a, items))
        relays = ep.setdefault("relays", {})
        for row in lead_seats(rows):
            repo, seat = seat_scope(row)
            if not in_scope(a, repo, seat):
                continue
            target = str(row.get("id"))
            rec = relays.get(target) or {}
            if rec.get("delivered_at") or rec.get("final"):
                continue
            resend = False
            if rec.get("record"):
                st = None if dry_run else status(relay_py, rec["record"])
                rec["record_state"] = st or rec.get("record_state")
                if st == "delivered":
                    rec["delivered_at"] = now.isoformat()
                    continue
                if st in ("failed", "expired") and not rec.get("resent"):
                    resend = True                              # one re-send per lead per episode
                elif st in ("failed", "expired", "cancelled", "missing"):
                    rec["final"] = st                          # not delivered; nothing left to do this episode
                    continue
                else:
                    continue                                   # queued, sending or unreadable: never re-send now
            elif rec:
                outcome = relay_outcome(rec.get("out"))
                if outcome is None:
                    started_at = parse_ts(rec.get("started_at"))
                    # a runner killed (or a reboot) before it wrote its outcome would read "running" forever: past its
                    # own bound plus slack it is abandoned and counts as never sent (local-review P2 on 4ef594c)
                    if started_at is None or (now - started_at).total_seconds() <= RELAY_RUN_TIMEOUT_S + 600:
                        continue                               # still running (an --idle wait)
                    outcome = {"rc": 124, "json": None}
                kind, rid = classify_send(outcome)
                rec["last_rc"] = outcome["rc"]
                rec["last_result"] = kind
                if kind == "delivered":
                    rec["delivered_at"] = now.isoformat()
                    continue
                if kind == "deferred":
                    rec["record"] = rid                        # followed through --status from the next run on
                    continue
                if kind == "unconfirmed":
                    rec["final"] = "unconfirmed"
                    continue
                if int(rec.get("attempts") or 0) >= MAX_RELAY_ATTEMPTS:
                    rec["final"] = "gave-up"
                    continue
            argv = relay_argv(relay_py, row, relay_text(a, now, n_work))
            actions.append({"episode": a.get("episode"), "action": "relay", "target": target, "argv": argv,
                            **({"resend": True} if resend else {})})
            if dry_run:
                continue
            attempt = int(rec.get("attempts") or 0) + 1
            out = str(state_path().parent / "relays" / f"{abs(hash((a['episode'], target, attempt))):x}-{attempt}.json")
            Path(out).parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
            try:
                Path(out).unlink()
            except FileNotFoundError:
                pass
            if relay(argv, out):
                new = {k: v for k, v in rec.items() if k not in ("record", "record_state", "last_result")}
                relays[target] = {**new, "attempts": attempt, "out": out, "started_at": now.isoformat(),
                                  **({"resent": True} if resend or rec.get("resent") else {})}
            elif rec:
                relays[target] = rec
    return actions


def pool_policy(policy: Policy, name: str) -> PoolPolicy | None:
    """The pool a lead names: a routing service (`opencode-go`, `antigravity-argon`) or an aiuse provider[/family]."""
    for (prov, fam), pp in policy.pools.items():
        if name in (pp.service, f"{prov}/{fam}" if fam else prov):
            return pp
    return None


# -- CLI ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

def run_check(args) -> tuple[int, list[dict], dict]:
    data = read_aiuse(args.live, args.input)
    if data is None:
        print("quota-surplus: no verdict: aiuse unreadable")
        return 3, [], {}
    now = now_utc()
    state = load_state(keep_aside=not args.dry_run)
    verdicts = assess(data, policy_from_routing(data.get("disabled_services")), now,
                      min_surplus=env_float("QUOTA_SURPLUS_MIN_SURPLUS", MIN_SURPLUS_PCT),
                      act_score=env_float("QUOTA_SURPLUS_ACT_SCORE", ACT_SCORE),
                      horizon_weekly_h=env_float("QUOTA_SURPLUS_HORIZON_WEEKLY_H", HORIZON_WEEKLY_H),
                      horizon_short_h=env_float("QUOTA_SURPLUS_HORIZON_SHORT_H", HORIZON_SHORT_H), state=state)
    record(state, verdicts, now)
    return 0, verdicts, state


def fmt_verdict(v: dict) -> str:
    head = f"{v['pool']:<28} {str(v.get('window') or ''):<26}"
    if v["verdict"] == "alert":
        return (f"{v['severity'].upper():<4} {head} {v['remaining_percent']:.0f}% left, ~{v['surplus']:.0f}% lost at "
                f"reset in {v['hours_left']:.1f}h (score {v['score']:g}){v.get('info_why') or ''}; "
                f"{v.get('dispatch') or ''}" + (" [notified]" if v.get("notified_at") else ""))
    tag = {"none": "ok", "skip": "skip", "no-verdict": "NO VERDICT"}[v["verdict"]]
    return f"{tag:<4} {head} {v.get('reason')}"


def main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:
    raw = sys.argv[1:] if argv is None else argv
    if raw[:1] == ["_relay-run"] and len(raw) >= 4 and raw[2] == "--":
        return relay_run(raw[1], raw[3:])          # internal: started by spawn_relay
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="quota-surplus", description=__doc__.split("\n\n")[0],
                                 formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter, epilog=__doc__)
    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest="cmd", required=True)
    for name in ("check", "notify"):
        p = sub.add_parser(name)
        p.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true", help="record nothing; notify sends nothing")
        p.add_argument("--live", action="store_true", help="aiuse --live (re-collect instead of its cache)")
        p.add_argument("--input", help="read aiuse JSON from FILE instead of running aiuse")
        if name == "check":
            p.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    lw = sub.add_parser("list-work")
    lw.add_argument("--repo", action="append", type=Path, help="repository directory (repeatable; default ~/src/*)")
    lw.add_argument("--fit", choices=["frontier", "bulk"])
    lw.add_argument("--pool", help="only items this pool (a service or provider/family) may serve, scope included")
    lw.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    args = ap.parse_args(argv)

    if args.cmd == "list-work":
        items = find_work([p.expanduser() for p in args.repo] if args.repo else None)
        if args.fit:
            items = [i for i in items if args.fit in i["fit"] or "any" in i["fit"]]
        if args.pool:
            pp = pool_policy(policy_from_routing({}), args.pool)
            if pp is None:
                print(f"quota-surplus: unknown pool {args.pool!r} (a routing service or provider/family)",
                      file=sys.stderr)
                return 2
            items = work_for({"frontier": pp.frontier, "allow_repos": list(pp.allow_repos),
                              "allow_seats": list(pp.allow_seats)}, items)
        if args.json:
            print(json.dumps(items, indent=2))
        else:
            for i in items:
                print(f"{i['repo']}#{i['n']} [{i.get('value', '?')}] {i['task']} | kind {i.get('kind', '?')} | size "
                      f"{i.get('size', '?')} | fit {','.join(i['fit'])} | {'read-only' if i['read_only'] else 'writes'}")
            if not items:
                print("no surplus work lists (docs/surplus-work.md) found" if not (args.fit or args.pool)
                      else "no surplus work item fits")
        return 0

    if args.dry_run:
        return run_and_report(args)
    # check and notify both read, change and replace the state file: hold one exclusive lock for the whole cycle so an
    # interactive check cannot erase a notify's notified_at/cooldown (local-review P2 on 28bd211)
    lock = state_lock(env_float("QUOTA_SURPLUS_LOCK_TIMEOUT", LOCK_TIMEOUT_S))
    if lock is None:
        print(f"quota-surplus: busy: another run holds {state_path()}.lock; nothing read, sent or recorded",
              file=sys.stderr)
        return 75
    with lock:
        return run_and_report(args)


def run_and_report(args) -> int:
    rc, verdicts, state = run_check(args)
    if rc:
        return rc
    now = now_utc()
    if args.cmd == "check":
        if args.json:
            print(json.dumps({"now": now.isoformat(), "verdicts": verdicts}, indent=2))
        else:
            for v in verdicts:
                print(fmt_verdict(v))
        if not args.dry_run:
            save_state(state)
        return 0
    actions = notify(verdicts, state, now, dry_run=args.dry_run,
                     renotify_h=env_float("QUOTA_SURPLUS_RENOTIFY_H", RENOTIFY_H))
    for a in actions:
        print(json.dumps(a))
    if not actions:
        print("quota-surplus: no new act episode")
    if not args.dry_run:
        save_state(state)
    return 0


def state_lock(timeout_s: float):
    """An open, exclusively flock'ed `<state>.lock` file (closing it releases the lock), or None after timeout_s."""
    p = Path(f"{state_path()}.lock")
    p.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    fh = p.open("a")
    deadline = time.monotonic() + max(0.0, timeout_s)
    while True:
        try:
            fcntl.flock(fh.fileno(), fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
            return fh
        except BlockingIOError:
            if time.monotonic() >= deadline:
                fh.close()
                return None
            time.sleep(0.2)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
